// [M-198-f4c-2-local-not-shadow-crossfile-topfn] — re-verified live 2026-07-17
// (Plan 212 pt.7). a.nv declares an ordinary top-level `fn f(y str) -> str`.
// b.nv binds a LOCAL `ro f = helper` (int->int) and calls `f(21)` — the
// local binding must shadow ANY sibling file's top-level `fn` of the same
// bare name, but checker resolve binds the call to a.nv's `f` instead.
//
// Current (2026-07-17) symptom: CODEGEN-FAIL —
//   error: [E7301] cannot pass `int` as argument `y` of type `str`
//   note: parameter `y` declared here --> a.nv:8:6   <- that's a.nv's fn f!
//
// Related (already tracked, different manifestation): [M-168-resize-with-free-fn-shadow]
// fixed the CLOSURE-PARAMETER case (Vec.resize_with/fill_with's `f` param);
// this is the LOCAL-VARIABLE case, still open.
//
// Quarantined here (fixtures/, walker-skip). Restore as a real (green) test
// once fixed.
module known_red.local_shadows_topfn

fn f(y str) -> str => "top-level-a:" + y

test "a: own top-level f(str) works" {
    assert(f("x") == "top-level-a:x")
}
